nd returns `{ content, conflicts }`.\n3. `src/index.ts` — the `DocumentStore` class and exported types/interfaces.\n\n### Data model inside `DocumentStore`\n- `branches: Map<string, Branch>`\n- `currentBranchName: string`\n- Global monotonic `snapshotId: number` incremented on every state-changing operation.\n\n`Branch` state:\n```ts\ninterface Branch {\n  docs: Map<string, object>;\n  history: Map<string, Version[]>; // version arrays per document id\n  snapshots: { id: number; docs: Record<string, object> }[];\n  parentBranch: string | null;\n  parentSnapshotId: number | null;\n}\n```\n- Every branch starts with a snapshot copied from its parent branch.\n- Each `create`, `update`, `delete`, and applied merge creates a new snapshot on the current branch.\n\n### Core operation details\n- **create(id, content)**: clones content, adds doc and initial version, snapshots.\n- **update(id, content)**: replaces content with clone, appends a version, snapshots.\n- **delete(id)**: removes doc from `docs` and clears history, snapshots empty state for that id.\n- **getHistory(id)**: returns chronological array; for correctness after history clear we keep doc deletion.\n- **getVersion(id, versionId)**: linear scan of history for matching version id.\n- **createBranch(name, fromBranch?)**: target defaults to current branch. Deep-clones source branch docs/history into new branch, records `parentBranch` and `parentSnapshotId` from source.\n- **switchBranch(name)**: validates existence, sets active branch.\n- **getBranch / listBranches**: straightforward.\n\n### Merge algorithm\n1. Find common ancestor branch by walking `parentBranch` chains of both current and source.\n2. Determine each branch's snapshot id on the common ancestor branch:\n   - If the branch is the common ancestor itself, use its latest snapshot id.\n   - Otherwise use the branch's `parentSnapshotId` for that ancestor chain.\n3. The merge base snapshot id is the earlier of the two on the common branch. Retrieve the